In @.planning/phases/43-fuse-write-durability/43-REVIEW.md around lines 29 - 244, This phase 43 code review identifies eight critical and nine warning-level issues that must be resolved before merge. Start by creating a resolution status document tracking disposition (fixed, deferred with ticket, or disputed) for each critical issue CR-01 through CR-08. For CR-01 in `fetch_merge_publish_parent` (crates/fuse/src/lib.rs:1080-1101), journal the user-ECIES-wrapped parent IPNS private key alongside the entry so replay can complete the publish, return Err until PublishResult::Success is confirmed, and remove the `unpin_content` call entirely—never unpin a CID that an active IPNS record references. For CR-02 in `replay_upload_entry` (crates/fuse/src/lib.rs:1195-1227), unwrap the journaled ECIES-wrapped file IPNS key using the user's private key before attempting the [u8; 32] conversion, and store the already-wrapped key in step 4 instead of re-wrapping it. For CR-03 in `write_ops.rs:525` and Windows equivalent, journal the user-wrapped key (`wrap_key(&ipns_private_key, &fs.public_key)`) in `child_ipns_key_hex` instead of the TEE-wrapped value, or store both as distinct fields if TEE-wrapped is needed separately. For CR-04 in `read_ops.rs:956-964` and Windows `write_ops.rs`, reply with `reply.error(libc::EIO)` and return early when the prepare closure (including `journal.put`) fails, after rolling back any inode state mutations. For CR-05 in `platform/windows/write_ops.rs:748-751`, correct the `UploadSpawnParams` struct to use `Arc<ApiClient>` (not `ApiConfig`), `tokio::runtime::Handle` (not `Arc<Runtime>`), and `Arc<crate::PublishCoordinator>` with proper module path, then add CI check for `cargo check --features winfsp`. For CR-06 in `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/fuse/windows/mod.rs`, call `replay_for_vault` before constructing `CipherBoxFS` (mirror the macOS path at fuse/mod.rs:233-242) and seed the Windows coordinator with initial sequences. For CR-07, inject the real journal directory into `SyncDaemon` (not the nonexistent `temp_dir/cipherbox-journal-default`), call `load_all_for_vault` in `sync_cycle` to detect pending/failed entries and emit `WriteParked` status, and have background upload failure paths call `record_failure`. For CR-08 in `read_ops.rs:941-943` and Windows equivalent, remove the journal entry only after the parent folder publish that includes this file's `file_meta_ipns_name` is confirmed (e.g., via a signal from the debounced publisher), and only when `publish_file_metadata` succeeded. Additionally address the warnings: WR-01 by sorting replay groups by `created_at_ms` before replay; WR-02 by recursively/BFS traversing folder metadata to resolve parent keys at arbitrary nesting depth; WR-03 by setting file permissions at creation time and fsyncing the journal directory; WR-04 by rolling back inode and parent-children state on prepare failure; WR-05 by threading journal entry IDs through conflict events to remove entries after successful re-armed publishes; WR-06 by storing file ciphertext in sidecar files with only path/hash in JSON and implementing GC for parked entries; WR-07 by wrapping replay in network timeouts matching the rest of the codebase; WR-08 by refusing to journal or replay UploadFile entries with empty `file_meta_ipns_name`. Document all resolutions with code changes and added tests before merge approval.","suggestions":[]}
